1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:04,237
(Howard:)Boy, oh, boy,
that's a lot of pieces.

2
00:00:04,238 --> 00:00:06,068
(Penny:)You know
what they all do, right?

3
00:00:06,073 --> 00:00:08,273
(Howard:)Yes, of course.

4
00:00:08,275 --> 00:00:09,745
(Sheldon:)What about this one?

5
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:12,513
(Leonard:)Well, I...
how familiar are you

6
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:15,013
(Howard:)with miniaturized
integrated logic circuits?

7
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:15,985
(Sheldon:)Not very.

8
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:17,153
(Howard:)That right there
is a miniaturized

9
00:00:17,151 --> 00:00:18,221
(Howard:)integrated logic circuit.

10
00:00:21,955 --> 00:00:23,625
(Sheldon:)So, can you
get it working?

11
00:00:23,624 --> 00:00:26,294
(Howard:)I'm an MIT-trained engineer.

12
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:28,793
(Howard:)I've built components
for the space station.

13
00:00:28,796 --> 00:00:32,336
(Sheldon:)I thought the zero-gravity
toilet didn't work.

14
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:34,003
(Howard:)It worked fine,

15
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:37,001
(Howard:)it just wasn't designed
for Russian cosmonauts

16
00:00:37,004 --> 00:00:39,604
(Howard:)and their potato-based diet.

17
00:00:39,607 --> 00:00:41,207
(Raj:)Hey, guys.

18
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:42,778
(Raj:)Hey.
Hello.

19
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:44,676
(Raj:)I have to return the helicopter.
My father...

20
00:00:44,678 --> 00:00:47,778
What did you do?!

21
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:50,178
(Sheldon:)Well, don't worry.

22
00:00:50,184 --> 00:00:51,654
(Sheldon:)He went to MIT.

23
00:00:51,652 --> 00:00:53,382
(Sheldon:)He can solve any problem,

24
00:00:53,387 --> 00:01:03,027
(Sheldon:)as long as it doesn't originate
in a Russian man's colon.

